    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_318a9825254eff15b28a54961949d923d8ac8e4ce80bd4cbba165796e5e7f3a1",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "In the absolutely convergent half-plane, unique factorization is represented by the Euler product; logarithmic differentiation and prime-power expansion convert that multiplicative representation into a von Mangoldt-weighted additive series, and the factored nonnegative trigonometric polynomial transfers positivity of those weights into an inequality coupling logarithmic derivatives at harmonically related heights.",
