    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_8dfd7c731de3b64f4708edd8793717d482fe64629922847308aa2612e3857c74",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The explicit Vinogradov-Korobov growth estimate and a tuned circle geometry provide complementary boundary control: the Euler-product lower bound handles the right semicircle, the growth upper bound handles the left, their cosine-weighted contributions are compressed to one log-power budget, and the circle identity converts that budget into logarithmic-derivative control with a retained reciprocal gap to a selected same-height zero.",
