      "proposed_content": "At the real-axis sample, the logarithmic derivative has controlled simple-pole-scale growth; a nonnegative trigonometric combination couples that term to four harmonic-height samples, where one circle estimate retains the hypothetical zero's reciprocal horizontal gap and the others contribute bounded losses. The resulting gap inequality is then optimized in the center displacement to produce a scale-matched zero-free width.",
